-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
UNDERLYING DATA
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Source: ClinicalTrials.gov, U.S. National Library of Medicine. Study records
are submitted by sponsors and investigators and are provided by NLM at no
charge. NLM's terms ask users of the data to attribute the source as
ClinicalTrials.gov, show the date the data were processed, and state any
modifications. This graph does so:

  * every study carries ex:sourceDataset "ClinicalTrials.gov", its
    ClinicalTrials.gov page (skos:exactMatch), ex:retrievedAt (download date)
    and ex:sourceVersionDate (NLM's processing date for the record);
  * modifications: records are converted to RDF; central contacts, site
    contacts and the results point of contact are omitted; e-mail addresses
    in any field are replaced with "[EMAIL REMOVED]"; free text is otherwise
    unchanged and never truncated.

NLM's terms also prohibit using e-mail addresses extracted from the database
for marketing. This graph contains none.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
THIRD-PARTY CONTENT EXCLUDED FROM THIS DEDICATION
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Adverse event terms reported by sponsors are often MedDRA terms (see
ex:sourceVocabulary). MedDRA is a trademark of ICH and its content is licensed
by the MSSO. MedDRA term text appears here only as submitted to and published
by ClinicalTrials.gov. It is not covered by this dedication; reuse of MedDRA
beyond that is subject to MSSO terms (https://www.meddra.org/).

NLM and ClinicalTrials.gov do not endorse this project.

